Usage: tac [OPTION]... [FILE]...

Concatenate and print files in reverse.

Write each FILE to standard output, last line first.
With no FILE, or when FILE is -, read standard input.

Records are separated by newline by default. Use -s to choose another separator,
-b to attach separators before records, and -r to treat the separator as a regex.


OPTIONS:
  -b, --before         attach the separator before instead of after each record
  -r, --regex          treat the separator as a regular expression
  -s, --separator ARG  use STRING as the record separator
      --help           display this help and exit
  -V, --version        output version information and exit

EXIT STATUS:
  0  if OK,
  1  if minor problems,
  2  if serious trouble.

WinuxCmd is a Windows implementation of GNU CoreUtils for Linux-Windows developers and AI coding assistants.
